SECTION 16. DISPUTE RESOLUTION

16.1 Any dispute, controversy or claim arising out of or in connection with
     this License or the Work, including any question regarding its existence,
     validity, interpretation, performance, breach or termination, and any
     non-contractual claim, shall be referred to and finally resolved by
     arbitration administered by the Baku Arbitration Centre (BAC, also
     referred to as Baku International Arbitration Centre) under its
     Arbitration Rules in force on the date on which the request for
     arbitration is filed, which Rules are deemed incorporated by reference.

16.2 The seat (legal place) of arbitration shall be Baku, Republic of
     Azerbaijan. The tribunal shall consist of one arbitrator, unless the
     amount in dispute exceeds the equivalent of AZN 500,000, in which case it
     shall consist of three arbitrators. The language of the arbitration shall
     be English. Expedited procedure provisions of the Rules apply where their
     conditions are met.

16.3 The law governing this arbitration agreement is the law of the Republic
     of Azerbaijan, including the Law of the Republic of Azerbaijan "On
     Arbitration". The award shall be final and binding, and judgment on it
     may be entered and enforced in any court having jurisdiction, including
     under the Convention on the Recognition and Enforcement of Foreign
     Arbitral Awards (New York, 1958).

16.4 Nothing in this Section prevents the Licensor from seeking interim or
     conservatory measures, including injunctions and the seizure of
     infringing copies, from any competent court, or from bringing
     infringement proceedings in the courts of any country in which an
     infringement occurs.

16.5 If You are a Consumer, this Section applies only to the extent permitted
     by mandatory law. A Consumer habitually resident in a Member State of the
     European Union may bring proceedings in, and may only be sued in, the
     courts of the Member State in which the Consumer is domiciled, in
     accordance with Articles 17 to 19 of Regulation (EU) No 1215/2012
     (Brussels I bis), unless an agreement entered into after the dispute has
     arisen provides otherwise.


